                    Senior Xero Accountant / Hands-On Operational Bookkeeper



Australian Construction and Maintenance Business | Part-Time | Long-Term



Build Technics is an established Melbourne commercial building-maintenance and repair business.



We are seeking an experienced Philippine-based Xero accountant who will personally own the accuracy and reliability of our Xero file.



This is not a tax-specialist role, a supervisory role or a detached management-accountant position. It combines hands-on bookkeeping and reconciliation with practical operational insight.



We need someone who can:



* keep Xero clean and fully reconciled;

* investigate discrepancies and unexplained balances;

* notice financial and operational patterns;

* connect accounting information with jobs and their actual stage;

* identify possible root causes;

* explain what matters in clear language;

* recommend practical next steps.



We do not want elaborate reports filled with financial ratios. We want concise, reliable information that helps us understand what is happening across jobs, cash flow and profitability.



## The role



You will initially help clean up and improve our Xero file and then take ongoing responsibility for weekly processing, reconciliations, month-end accounts and operational-finance reporting.



You will personally complete the work. This role must not be subcontracted, delegated or passed to another member of a bookkeeping team.



## Hands-on Xero responsibilities



You will be responsible for work including:



* reviewing and coding transactions;

* bank and credit-card reconciliations;

* accounts receivable and accounts payable review;

* payment and clearing-account reconciliations;

* reviewing GST coding and identifying exceptions;

* reconciling payroll and superannuation liabilities;

* reviewing loans, prepayments, accruals, fixed assets and suspense accounts;

* correcting miscodings and investigating unexplained balances;

* checking that receipts, invoices and supporting documents are present;

* month-end journals and balance-sheet reconciliation;

* maintaining clear reconciliation workpapers;

* preparing a concise month-end exception list;

* working with our current Xero and OFX/payment processes.



Our Australian BAS/payroll agent retains responsibility for payroll, superannuation, BAS and specialist GST review. You will provide clean, reconciled information and raise issues requiring their attention.



## Operational and commercial insight



Completing the reconciliation is not the end of the job.



We expect you to look at what the accounting records are telling us about the business.



You should notice:



* unusual balances and changing trends;

* recurring coding or documentation errors;

* completed work that has not been invoiced;

* invoices delayed by client approval or portal requirements;

* supplier costs paid before corresponding client receipts;

* customer deposits received for work not yet completed;

* supplier deposits and prepayments relating to unfinished jobs;

* jobs accumulating costs without sufficient revenue;

* deteriorating margins;

* recurring client, supplier or process issues;

* clearing or suspense balances that repeatedly return;

* financial information that reconciles mathematically but does not make commercial sense.



When raising an issue, we would like you to explain:



1. What you noticed.

2. Why it appears unusual or important.

3. The likely cause or possible explanations.

4. The financial or operational effect.

5. What you recommend checking or changing.

6. Who needs to take the next action.



You are not expected to have every answer or make decisions outside your authority. However, you should bring considered observations and possible solutions—not simply pass unexplained problems to someone else.



## WIP, larger jobs and cash exposure



Most of our work involves relatively straightforward maintenance jobs. We do not require complicated WIP calculations for every small job.



For material unfinished jobs—generally jobs above approximately AUD $15,000—we want a simple operational-finance overview showing information such as:



* expected job or contract value;

* customer deposits invoiced and received;

* supplier deposits and costs paid;

* approximate stage of completion;

* revenue and costs currently appearing in Xero;

* remaining supplier commitments;

* work completed but not yet invoiced;

* estimated amount remaining to invoice;

* expected or forecast margin;

* current cash exposure.



We want someone capable of identifying when revenue, costs, cash and the actual stage of a job are telling different stories.



## Working with the local team



You will work with:



* the Directors, who make commercial and financial decisions;

* our Australian BAS/payroll agent, who handles BAS, payroll, super and specialist treatments;

* our local Business Support & Operations Lead, who obtains job-stage information and follows up operational actions;

* administrative support staff who can locate receipts, invoices and other documents.



Your role is to validate and explain the financial position.



The local Business Support & Operations Lead will then investigate operational circumstances, make calls, allocate actions and follow through with clients, suppliers, trades and coordinators.



For example, you might report:



> “Five jobs have a combined AUD $43,000 pre-funded cash exposure, and three appear substantially complete but have not yet been invoiced.”



The local lead then establishes what is preventing invoicing, who owns each action and when it will be resolved.



## Analytical ownership and continuous improvement



We value someone who:



* investigates rather than merely clears discrepancies;

* distinguishes isolated errors from recurring problems;

* looks for the process creating the accounting issue;

* identifies trends across jobs, clients and reporting periods;

* raises issues early;

* explains information in plain English;

* suggests simple improvements;

* follows material issues through until resolved or formally handed over;

* is honest about errors, uncertainty and missing information;

* takes personal ownership of the quality of the file.



A useful observation with a practical recommendation is more valuable to us than a large, polished report.



## Job-management-system experience



Experience with job-management or field-service systems is highly regarded—particularly Simpro or AroFlo, as well as ServiceM8, Tradify, Fergus, Ascora, Buildertrend, Procore or similar platforms.



We are especially interested in candidates who have used these systems alongside Xero to understand:



* job costing;

* work in progress;

* purchase orders;

* supplier costs;

* deposits and progress claims;

* unbilled work;

* invoicing stages;

* job profitability.



We currently use ServiceM8 and expect our job-management and reporting capability to become more sophisticated over time. Simpro or AroFlo experience would be particularly valuable but is not essential.



## Required experience and qualities



We are looking for someone with:



* substantial hands-on Xero bookkeeping and accounting experience;

* experience working with Australian businesses;

* experience inside an Australian accounting/bookkeeping firm or directly within an Australian operating business;

* strong month-end and whole-balance-sheet reconciliation capability;

* understanding of Australian GST, BAS, payroll and superannuation accounts;

* experience with customer deposits, supplier prepayments, accruals and clearing accounts;

* confidence investigating unusual balances and coding;

* clear written and spoken English;

* strong judgement, curiosity and attention to detail;

* the ability to work independently and communicate proactively;

* a reliable and secure home-office setup;

* a genuine interest in a stable, long-term relationship.



An accounting degree, CPA qualification and Xero certification are highly regarded. Practical ability, ownership and operational thinking are more important than tax-specialist credentials alone.



Experience with construction, trades, maintenance, field services or another job-based business will be highly regarded.



## Hours and rate



* Initial clean-up and establishment period: approximately 10–12 hours per week, potentially slightly higher for short periods if agreed.

* Likely ongoing requirement: approximately 8–10 hours per week.

* Preferred working pattern: blocks on Monday and Tuesday so information is available for our Wednesday team meeting, with a shorter Thursday block if required.

* Some regular overlap with Melbourne business hours is required.

* Rate: approximately AUD $10–$17 per hour, depending on demonstrated capability and experience.

* This is intended to be a stable, ongoing part-time engagement.



Please apply only if these hours are genuinely worthwhile for you over the longer term.



## How to apply



Start your application with:



**BT XERO**



Do not send only a generic cover letter. Please answer every question below in numbered order.



Specific, factual answers are more useful than polished general statements.



1. How many years have you personally worked with Australian businesses in Xero?



2. Have you worked directly inside an Australian accounting or bookkeeping firm, or inside an Australian operating business? Name the type of organisation and explain the work you personally completed.



3. Describe the balance-sheet accounts you normally reconcile at month end.



4. Briefly explain how you would treat:



   * a customer commencement deposit for unfinished work; and

   * a 50% supplier deposit for an unfinished job.



   Include the broad GST and management-reporting considerations.



5. Give one specific example where you noticed an accounting discrepancy or financial trend that led you to identify a recurring operational or process problem. Explain:



   * what you noticed;

   * how you investigated it;

   * the root cause;

   * what you recommended;

   * the result.



6. For a construction and maintenance business, what would you include in a simple monthly operational-finance overview covering larger unfinished jobs, WIP, deposits, unbilled work, cash exposure and likely margin?



7. Have you used Simpro, AroFlo, ServiceM8 or another job-management or field-service platform? State:



   * the system;

   * how long you used it;

   * the business or industry;

   * exactly what you personally did;

   * whether you used it for job costing, WIP, purchase orders, supplier costs, deposits, progress claims, invoicing or job-profitability reporting;

   * how you compared or reconciled its information with Xero.



   If you have not used one, please simply say so.



8. State your current employment, normal working hours and number of other private clients. Confirm whether outside client work is permitted and whether you are continuing to seek full-time employment.



9. Confirm that you will personally perform and review all Build Technics work and will not subcontract, delegate or share access with another person.



10. Confirm whether you can provide:



* 10–12 hours per week initially;

* approximately 8–10 hours per week ongoing;

* Monday and Tuesday working blocks;

* some overlap with Melbourne business hours.



11. State your expected sustainable hourly rate in AUD.



12. Attach your résumé, Xero certification and details of your accounting qualification. Please also confirm whether an Australian manager or client can provide a reference covering your technical work and reliability.



Shortlisted candidates will be invited to complete a standard paid practical assessment using synthetic accounting and job information.



We are looking for a hands-on Xero accountant with operational and commercial curiosity—not simply a tax specialist and not a detached management accountant.
